[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/q3k3/1np1bpp1/3p2b1/1p1Pp1P1/1P2P3/2P5/2BN1P2/2B1K2Q_b_-_-_0_22"]

{ This time your queen does the work. Look along his back row before you move. }
22... Bxg5 { He grabs a pawn with the bishop. His king and his queen share a row. } 23. Qh8+ { Check all the way down the row. He must move, and his queen cannot follow. [%cal Gh8e8,Ge8a8] } (23. Nb3 { A sensible knight move, and the moment quietly passes. } 23... Bxc1 24. Nxc1 Nd8 { Level, and his queen in the corner is perfectly safe. }) (23. Bd3 { You tidy your pieces up and he simply walks the king away. } 23... Ke7 { Now there is nothing behind the king and the idea has gone. }) 23... Ke7 { The king steps off the row, and everything behind him is loose. } 24. Qxa8 { A whole queen, collected from the far corner. } (24. Qh3 { You bring the queen home instead of collecting. } 24... Nd8 25. Qg4 { His queen is safe and you are the one who is worse. }) 1-0


