{ Almost nothing left on the board. Your bishop and his king and knight sit on one line. }
33. Nd1 { The knight drops back. Now his king and his knight share a diagonal. } 33... Bh5+ { Check from far away, and the knight behind him cannot move. [%cal Gh5f3,Gf3d1] } (33... Kd6 { A quiet king step. But his knight is loose right this moment. } 34. Ne3 Ke6 35. Kg3 { The chance has gone and this is only a draw. }) (33... Bg6 { The bishop steps out, but it arrives without check. } 34. Kg3 { No check means he simply walks over and defends the knight. }) 34. Kg2 { The king moves aside. Look all the way down the diagonal. } 34... Bxd1 { A whole knight, won from the other side of the board. } (34... Bg6 { You tuck the bishop away and the knight escapes. } 35. Kh3 Kd6 36. Nf2 { The knight is safe and the game is a draw. }) 0-1


[Event "Basic tactics: the discovered attack, lesson"]
[Result "0-1"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/oLCBkefa/Wo1dJhaW"]
[FEN "8/pp4k1/3r2pp/4N3/3n3P/6P1/P2R2PK/8 w - - 10 41"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/8/pp4k1/3r2pp/4N3/3n3P/6P1/P2R2PK/8_w_-_-_10_41"]

{ We will now learn the discovered attack. One piece moves away and another one strikes. }
41. Nf3 { His knight offers a trade. Notice that your own knight blocks your rook. [%csl Gd6,Rd2][%cal Yd4f3] } 41... Nxf3+ { Your knight leaves with check, and the rook behind it wakes up. [%cal Gd6d2] } (41... Nf5 { You save the knight, but the rook behind it never gets going. } 42. Rb2 b6 43. Rc2 { Nothing has happened here. This is a draw. }) (41... h5 { A pawn move, and he untangles at once. } 42. Nxd4 { He simply takes your knight and the chance has gone. }) 42. gxf3 { He must answer the check first. That is the whole idea. [%cal Yd6d2] } 42... Rxd2+ { A free rook. The check bought you the time to take it. } (42... Ra6 { The rook goes the wrong way and the moment passes. } 43. Rd7+ Kf6 44. Rxb7 { Now he is the one collecting pawns. }) 0-1


[Event "Basic tactics: discovered attack practice one"]
[Result "0-1"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/oLCBkefa/q1pQjWr0"]
