[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/3r2k1/1pp2pp1/p2b3p/8/1P6/P3P3/4NPPP/3R2K1_w_-_-_0_21"]

{ Your rook and his rook face each other down one column, and your bishop is in the way. }
21. h3 { He makes a little space for his king. Your bishop is standing in your own way. } 21... Bh2+ { The bishop leaves the column with check, and offers itself as well. [%cal Gd8d1] } (21... c5 { A pawn push while the two rooks stare at each other. } 22. Nc3 cxb4 23. axb4 { Even, and the trick has quietly gone. }) (21... Be7 { The bishop does step off the column, but far too slowly. } 22. Nd4 { He gets organised and his rook is defended again. }) 22. Kxh2 { He takes the bishop, and his king has left the back rank. } 22... Rxd1 { A bishop for a rook, because his king had to answer the check first. } (22... Ra8 { You forget to take, and a whole piece is gone for nothing. } 23. Nd4 c6 24. Nb3 { A bishop down with nothing at all to show. }) 0-1


[Event "Basic tactics: the back rank mate, lesson"]
[Result "1-0"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/oLCBkefa/4UUeXlma"]
[FEN "7k/1p4pp/p1b5/8/6N1/7P/PP1R1K2/4r3 b - - 4 38"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/7k/1p4pp/p1b5/8/6N1/7P/PP1R1K2/4r3_b_-_-_4_38"]

{ We will now learn the back rank mate. A king with pawns in front of it has no air. }
38... Rb1 { His king is stuck behind its own two pawns. Send your rook to the last row. [%csl Rh8,Rg7,Rh7][%cal Yd2d8] } 39. Rd8+ { Check, and his king has nowhere to run. Only a block can delay it. [%cal Gd8h8] } (39. Ne5 { A fine square for the knight, but the mate was already on. } 39... g6 40. Nxc6 bxc6 { You traded pieces and gave his king a breathing hole. }) (39. h4 { You make air for your own king and hand him the time. } 39... h6 { Now his king has a square too, and the mate has gone. }) 39... Be8 { He throws the bishop in the way. Take it. [%cal Yd8e8] } 40. Rxe8# { Mate. The pawns he never moved are what trapped him. } (40. b3 { You had mate in one and pushed a pawn instead. } 40... Rb2+ 41. Kf3 { The mate is still there, but so is his rook. }) 1-0


[Event "Basic tactics: back rank practice one"]
[Result "1-0"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/oLCBkefa/vkwgJUeX"]
[FEN "r1b1q2k/ppp3pp/3R4/8/8/4PQ2/P5PP/5RK1 b - - 0 19"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r1b1q2k/ppp3pp/3R4/8/8/4PQ2/P5PP/5RK1_b_-_-_0_19"]

{ His king is boxed in again, but this time a defender is guarding the door. }
19... cxd6 { He takes your rook and you are a whole rook down. His queen guards f8. [%csl Rh8,Rg7,Rh7] } 20. Qf8+ { The queen walks in anyway. She cannot be ignored and she cannot be allowed. [%cal Gf3f8] } (20. Rf2 { You defend instead of striking, and now you are simply losing. } 20... Be6 21. Qxb7 Bg8 { His extra rook decides the game. }) (20. h3 { A quiet move, and the whole idea evaporates. } 20... Bd7 21. Qxb7 Bc6 { He is a rook up and getting organised. }) 20... Qxf8 { He has to take. His queen is no longer guarding that square. } 21. Rxf8# { Mate. You gave a queen to drag his guard off the last row. } (21. Rf2 { You forget the mate and hand the queen straight back. } 21... Qxf2+ 22. Kxf2 { A queen down instead of mate in one. }) 1-0


[Event "Basic tactics: removing the defender, lesson"]
[Result "1-0"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/oLCBkefa/qSjhztze"]
[FEN "r5k1/5ppp/4q3/p7/1pQ1P3/P2P3P/KP6/2R5 b - - 3 28"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r5k1/5ppp/4q3/p7/1pQ1P3/P2P3P/KP6/2R5_b_-_-_3_28"]

{ We will now learn to remove the defender. Take away the guard, then take the prize. }
28... Rc8 { His rook comes to your column. Only his queen defends it from e6. [%csl Rc8][%cal Ge6c8] } 29. Qxe6 { Take the guard first, even though it is a queen for a queen. [%cal Yc4e6] } (29. axb4 { You grab a pawn, and his rook lands on your queen instead. } 29... Rxc4 30. dxc4 axb4 { A rook for nothing, and you are lost. }) (29. Rc2 { You defend the queen, and he simply takes her anyway. } 29... Rxc4 30. dxc4 { The queen has gone and so has the game. }) 29... fxe6 { He takes back. The guard is gone and the rook is loose. [%cal Yc1c8] } 30. Rxc8+ { A whole rook. Remove the defender, then collect. } (30. Rb1 { You forget the rook you paid a queen to win. } 30... bxa3 31. Kxa3 { Level again, and the queen was spent for nothing. }) 1-0


[Event "Basic tactics: removing the defender practice one"]
[Result "0-1"]
